{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-20239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ on $X?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-20239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & -1+(-3)(2) & 1+(-3)(1) \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-20239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-20239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-20239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-20239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $B?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4+(4)(1) & 12+(4)(3) & 3+(4)(6) \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1+1 & 2+3 & 4+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-10245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10245" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {