fd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $X?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & 5+(-1)(3) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(1) \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-72760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capt