 ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5+(-1)(5) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(-1) & 1+(-1)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-10217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-10217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:=(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 6 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot (-3) & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 9 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130071" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-130071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -\\frac{8}{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130071" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $U?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1 & -3+0 & 4+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72786" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-72786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-72786" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4+(-1)(-1) & 4+(-1)(9) & 6+(-1)(-2) & 7+(-1)(6) \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130072" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-130072" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio