{"question" "q-130095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=3\\cdot {R}_{1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1d3886a32f041ff3d54ead8d7bedf6ee51066c77018660135ca1dc42931a9d61"} {"question" "q-130095" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e1075987ba2cc1c738cd69eb3f141026ad1aef5cfd27a7c0ca679e1a"} {"question" "q-130095" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{R}_{1}:=3\\cdot {R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{1}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-\\frac{4}{7})\\cdot {R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}"] ["math" "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038539/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c0d6d44e107598